<title>POLAND: Pioneer takes part of Tonsil share offer.</title>
<headline>Pioneer takes part of Tonsil share offer.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tohoku Pioneer Electronic Corporation bought 20,000 of 60,000 shares of Tonsil SA offered in the speaker system maker's new share issue which ended on January 12, Tonsil said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said Pioneer did not buy the remaining 40,000 shares because of an unfavourable yen/dollar exchange rate.</p>
<p>Tonsil's management also gave 450,000 shares to the state treasury in exchange for 7.8 million zloty debt and 80,000 shares to Krzysztof Niezgoda for a 1.45 million zloty debt.</p>
<p>After the issue Tonsil will have 3.4 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
